#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Sea Lion: Kent and Sussex, September 1940.  A sample game for the
Grognard engine, and an invasion that never happened.

In the summer of 1940 the German army planned to cross the Channel in
river barges towed by tugs and land on the beaches between Folkestone
and Bexhill: Operation Sea Lion.  It was put off when the Luftwaffe
failed to win the air over England, and never tried.  Here it is tried:
the first wave lands at dawn, and the rest must come across a Channel
the Royal Navy still commands.  Play either side against the computer,
or against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./sealion (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.sealion.json.  ./sealion --selftest checks the map and
plays a game between two computer players.
"""

